WEBVTT

00:03:56.148 --> 00:04:00.194
20 years ago, if you said
the term "lost decade,"

00:04:00.194 --> 00:04:01.737
you were talking about Japan.

00:04:01.779 --> 00:04:04.907
My apologies to anybody here
of Japanese heritage.

00:04:04.949 --> 00:04:08.244
Today, it's an appropriate term
for much of the global economy.

00:04:08.244 --> 00:04:11.038
From Britain to Italy,
South Africa to Brazil,

00:04:11.038 --> 00:04:13.666
as one lost decade becomes two.

00:04:14.542 --> 00:04:16.002
And it gets worse.

00:04:16.836 --> 00:04:20.548
This economic malaise
we've seen over the last 15 years

00:04:20.589 --> 00:04:23.134
is surely to be joined
by the climate crisis,

00:04:23.134 --> 00:04:26.512
and then, demographic aging,
a crisis of elderly care.

00:04:26.512 --> 00:04:30.308
It turns out that the opening decades
of the 21st century,